\b Brunei Finance App MVP Wireframe Spec\b0\par
\par
\b Screen 1: Landing Page\b0\par
Purpose: introduce the product and drive sign up.\par
Content:\par
- app name and short value proposition\par
- hero section\par
- key benefits\par
- features overview\par
- sign up and log in buttons\par
\par
\b Screen 2: Sign Up\b0\par
Fields:\par
- full name\par
- email\par
- password\par
- confirm password\par
CTA: Create account\par
\par
\b Screen 3: Log In\b0\par
Fields:\par
- email\par
- password\par
CTA: Log in\par
Secondary link: Forgot password\par
\par
\b Screen 4: Onboarding Step 1 - Welcome\b0\par
Purpose: explain what the app will help with.\par
Content:\par
- quick intro\par
- 3-step summary of setup\par
CTA: Start setup\par
\par
\b Screen 5: Onboarding Step 2 - Salary and Payday\b0\par
Fields:\par
- monthly salary\par
- payday day of month\par
CTA: Continue\par
\par
\b Screen 6: Onboarding Step 3 - Commitments\b0\par
Fields per commitment:\par
- name\par
- amount\par
- due day optional\par
CTA:\par
- Add another commitment\par
- Continue\par
\par
\b Screen 7: Onboarding Step 4 - Debts\b0\par
Fields per debt:\par
- debt type\par
- lender\par
- outstanding balance\par
- monthly payment\par
- rate optional\par
CTA:\par
- Add another debt\par
- Continue\par
\par
\b Screen 8: Onboarding Step 5 - Categories\b0\par
Purpose: confirm default budgeting categories.\par
Content:\par
- checklist of starter categories\par
- allow add custom category later\par
CTA: Finish setup\par
\par
\b Screen 9: Dashboard\b0\par
Purpose: main home screen after login.\par
Sections:\par
- top summary cards:\par
  - monthly income\par
  - commitments\par
  - spent this month\par
  - remaining amount\par
- debt summary card\par
- top spending categories chart\par
- recent transactions list\par
- insights cards\par
- quick actions:\par
  - add transaction\par
  - upload statement\par
  - add debt\par
\par
\b Screen 10: Transactions List\b0\par
Purpose: review all transactions.\par
Content:\par
- search bar\par
- filters: date, category, account, type\par
- transaction table\par
- add transaction button\par
Actions:\par
- edit\par
- delete\par
\par
\b Screen 11: Add/Edit Transaction\b0\par
Fields:\par
- date\par
- amount\par
- type debit/credit\par
- merchant\par
- description\par
- category\par
- account\par
- notes\par
CTA: Save transaction\par
\par
\b Screen 12: Monthly Budget Page\b0\par
Purpose: set and review budget allocations.\par
Content:\par
- month selector\par
- budget rows by category\par
- planned amount\par
- actual amount\par
- variance\par
- total planned vs salary\par
CTA: Save budget\par
\par
\b Screen 13: Commitments Page\b0\par
Purpose: manage recurring monthly obligations.\par
Content:\par
- commitments table\par
- add/edit/delete commitment\par
- monthly total summary\par
\par
\b Screen 14: Debts Page\b0\par
Purpose: view all debts in one place.\par
Content:\par
- total monthly debt payment\par
- debt-to-income ratio\par
- list of debts\par
- add debt button\par
\par
\b Screen 15: Debt Detail / Payoff Simulator\b0\par
Purpose: help user understand payoff options.\par
Content:\par
- debt summary\par
- outstanding balance\par
- monthly payment\par
- optional rate\par
- input field for extra monthly payment\par
- projected payoff comparison\par
CTA: Save scenario\par
\par
\b Screen 16: Statement Upload\b0\par
Purpose: upload local bank statements.\par
Content:\par
- select bank type\par
- file upload field\par
- support note for BIBD and Baiduri PDFs\par
- privacy note\par
CTA: Upload and parse\par
\par
\b Screen 17: Statement Review\b0\par
Purpose: review parsed transactions before import.\par
Content:\par
- uploaded file summary\par
- parsed transactions table\par
- editable category column\par
- confidence/error flags\par
CTA:\par
- confirm import\par
- cancel\par
\par
\b Screen 18: Insights Page\b0\par
Purpose: show monthly financial observations.\par
Content:\par
- top spending insight\par
- debt burden insight\par
- trend insight\par
- before-payday estimate\par
- category overspend warnings\par
\par
\b Screen 19: Profile and Settings\b0\par
Content:\par
- name\par
- email\par
- payday\par
- monthly salary\par
- category management\par
- account preferences\par
- sign out\par
\par
\b Screen 20: Premium Page\b0\par
Purpose: explain upgrade value.\par
Content:\par
- premium features list\par
- statement import\par
- debt simulation\par
- advanced insights\par
- pricing placeholder\par
CTA: Upgrade\par
\par
\b Layout Guidance\b0\par
- left sidebar navigation on desktop\par
- top nav on mobile\par
- dashboard-first experience\par
- use cards and clean spacing\par
- keep forms short and focused\par
- use calm colors and trust-oriented design\par
\par
\b Design Tone\b0\par
The interface should feel trustworthy, modern, simple, and practical. Think calm fintech dashboard rather than complex accounting software.\par
}